// An element of an array literal is handed off to the array. A named `string` there says which hand-off it means
// — `give s` or `copy s` — as it does in `xs.add(item: …)`; bare, it would be two owners of one buffer.
fn int32 main() {
    string s = "a heap-backed string, long enough to leave any inline buffer";
    InlineArray<string>#(2) a = [s, "y"];
    return 0;
}
